From: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] BiosDxe: consume pending settings without a history record

HandleResource() only consumes /Systems/1/Bios/Settings when
RedfishGetConfigLanguage() finds a ConfigLangMap record persisted by a
PREVIOUS boot. Without one it declares "system reset detected", skips the
consume, and says so only at DEBUG_MANAGEABILITY - invisible in this
platform's RELEASE build. The staged attributes on the BMC are neither
applied nor deleted, and the operator gets no signal at all.

Upstream's rationale is that a missing record means a reset-to-defaults,
after which the BMC's staged values might be stale. Neither half holds
here: the record can be missing for benign reasons (first boot with the
client feature layer, a replaced SD card, any loss of the RedfishClient
variables), this board has no defaulting command that wipes the variable
store behind the BMC's back, and the staged set is always current
operator intent. The cost of the skip is the exact reported failure -
"the Bios settings are staged in nanokvm-app but never applied" - while
the cost of consuming is zero: the identify step immediately above has
already rebuilt the in-memory ConfigLangMap that the consume path needs.

Consume unconditionally; keep the detection only as a breadcrumb.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform policy]
Signed-off-by: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
--- a/RedfishClientPkg/Features/Bios/v1_1_0/Common/BiosCommon.c
+++ b/RedfishClientPkg/Features/Bios/v1_1_0/Common/BiosCommon.c
@@ -971,17 +971,24 @@
   }
 
   //
-  // Consume first.
+  // Consume first. Upstream skips the pending settings when no history
+  // record exists (SystemResetDetected), treating such a boot as a
+  // reset-to-defaults whose staged values may be stale. On this platform
+  // the staged set is always live operator intent held by the BMC, no
+  // defaulting command wipes the variable store behind it, and the skip is
+  // invisible in a RELEASE build - a boot without history would silently
+  // discard the operator's staged settings. Consume unconditionally: the
+  // identify step above already populated the in-memory ConfigLangMap,
+  // which is everything the consume path needs.
   //
   if (SystemResetDetected) {
-    DEBUG ((DEBUG_MANAGEABILITY, "%a: System has been reset to the default setting. Ignore the pending settings and don't consume it because they may be the stale values.\n", __func__));
-    DEBUG ((DEBUG_MANAGEABILITY, "%a: Skip the consume porcess.\n", __func__));
-  } else {
-    DEBUG ((DEBUG_MANAGEABILITY, "%a: Consume for %s\n", __func__, Uri));
-    Status = EdkIIRedfishResourceConfigConsume (&SchemaInfo, Uri, NULL);
-    if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
-      DEBUG ((DEBUG_ERROR, "%a: Failed to consume resource for: %s: %r\n", __func__, Uri, Status));
-    }
+    DEBUG ((DEBUG_MANAGEABILITY, "%a: no history record (first boot or reset); consuming pending settings anyway\n", __func__));
+  }
+
+  DEBUG ((DEBUG_MANAGEABILITY, "%a: Consume for %s\n", __func__, Uri));
+  Status = EdkIIRedfishResourceConfigConsume (&SchemaInfo, Uri, NULL);
+  if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
+    DEBUG ((DEBUG_ERROR, "%a: Failed to consume resource for: %s: %r\n", __func__, Uri, Status));
   }
 
   //
